{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>Take heed to yourselves, lest you make a graven image.</b> He has already said the like. The reason is to add 'a consuming fire; therefore I command you' (in the preceding verse)." "<b>The form of anything.</b> Any thing." "<b>That He commanded you.</b> Either 'as He commanded you,' or the word צוך is in the sense of not doing, as in 'and upon the clouds I will command' (Psalm 68:5 — i.e., the command is a prohibition). Some say it refers to the forms of the stars. This is far-fetched in my eyes."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:22:15.976725757Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}